  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SURVIVAL PLUSS: Mama-baby survival in Uganda and South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aimed to improve mama-baby survival by promoting universal access to and utilization of already, freely available maternity and child health inteventions such as facility based delivery and childhood vacccines. The project has implemented a teaching/training program with a focus on maternal and child health (MMED Pediatrics, PhD and training of &quot;pregnancy buddies&quot;) and reserach involving students and staff at University of Juba, Gulu University and Busitema University, Makerere University as agreement partner and University of Bergen as Norwegian partner institution.</narrative>
  </description>
